## When to use brainstorming

Load `brainstorming` for explicit brainstorming or design-option requests, including
「ブレストしたい」「案を比較したい」「方針を一緒に決めたい」, even when the user is not asking
for implementation. Also load it when a requested change leaves an important choice about intended
behavior, scope, constraints, or side effects unresolved. Compare viable options before committing
to one; ask only when a consequential choice actually requires the user.

Skip brainstorming for a settled local change or a routine, reversible implementation detail.
An unknown bug cause calls for `systematic-debugging`, not brainstorming. A design-only request
does not authorize implementation, and loading brainstorming does not require delegation.

## Pi runtime

Read `pi-runtime` before launching another agent or handing off work. Use the shared Agent Selection policy; being in Pi does not make Pi the default for new sessions.

